  "articleBody": "A well-planned pantry should match your household’s shopping habits, appliance storage needs, available floor area, and kitchen workflow. A cabinet pantry often preserves more kitchen space and keeps ingredients close at hand, while a walk-in pantry can hold bulk goods and countertop appliances. The right choice depends on layout, accessibility, construction scope, and how the space will be used.",
